<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaMazon U'Mayim Acharonim — Halachah 4<br>Part 1 of 3 (§§ 1–9)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE FULL TRANSLATION</span></div>
<div class="lm">Based on <span class="lr">LM II:40</span> — <span class="v">"Mi She'yodai'a Mai'Eretz Yisrael"</span><br>Whoever knows of Eretz Yisrael; his'pa'arus; the cup of blessing; Chanukah</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Halachic framework</span>: Based on the <span class="h">Torah</span> <span class="v">"Whoever knows of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>,"</span> etc. (<span class="lr">Likutay Tinyana, Siman 40</span>) — see there, the entire <span class="h">Torah</span> well.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 1 — The Holiness of <i>Eretz Yisrael</i> Through <i>His'pa'arus</i></div>

<div class="p">The general principle: The essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is through <span class="v">"the eyes of Hashem"</span> — through Hashem constantly gazing there — through which <span class="mx">"the air of Eretz Yisrael makes wise,"</span> for eyes are associated with <span class="h">chochmah</span> [wisdom]. The essential aspect of "the eyes of Hashem" is aroused through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> [glorification] that Hashem takes in Israel, in the aspect of <span class="v">"Yisrael, in whom I take pride [<span class="h">espa'ir</span>]."</span> This is the aspect of <span class="h">tefillin</span>, etc.</div>

<div class="p">Whoever gazes upon this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — in him too there are formed the aspect of <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">tefillin</span>, and the <span class="h">mochin</span> break through into the eyes. Then wherever he gazes, the air becomes the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as above. However, the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of Hashem Himself — not everyone merits to see. But one who gazes upon the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, and especially at the time when the world gathers to him — i.e. on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span>, when the essential gathering takes place — then much <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> ascends from the aforementioned gathering of those who come together for the sake of serving Hashem. And the <span class="h">tzadik</span> is comprised of all this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, for the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem takes in Israel is through the <span class="h">tzadik</span> who draws them close to Hashem — through which Hashem takes pride in them.</div>

<div class="p">It emerges that the <span class="h">tzadik</span> himself is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. Therefore whoever gazes with his eyes upon the <span class="h">tzadik</span> draws upon himself also from this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — the aspect of <span class="h">tefillin</span> — and then the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and <span class="h">mochin</span> break through into the eyes. Then wherever this person gazes, <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed as well, for the essential [holiness of] <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed through the eyes drawn through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, etc., as above — see all this there well.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 2 — The Cup of <i>Birchas HaMazon</i>: Gazing at <i>His'pa'arus</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of: the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — one must place one's eyes upon it. For the essence of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> is to reveal the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, from which the essential holiness and <span class="h">tikkun</span> of eating [derives], as explained elsewhere (above in <span class="h">Hilchos Devarim HaNohagin BiS'udah</span> — see there). As it is written: <span class="v">"and you shall eat and be satisfied, and you shall bless Hashem your G-d for the good land that He gave you."</span> The essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is revealed through the eyes — through gazing upon the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of Israel, as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> after the eating of Israel. For the cup of blessing is the aspect of the totality of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that which Hashem takes pride in Israel — through which great joy and delight are made in all the worlds. For conversely, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>, when one of Israel falls from his <span class="h">avodah</span>, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span> — the aspect of <span class="v">"and He was grieved in His heart."</span> As our Sages <span class="h">zichronam livrachah</span> said: <span class="mx">"What does the Shechinah say? 'My head is heavy upon Me, My arm is heavy upon Me.'"</span> As this teaching is brought in the aforementioned <span class="h">Torah</span>.</div>

<div class="p">But conversely — when Israel draws close to Hashem and He takes pride in them — then strength and delight are added in all the worlds, in the aspect of <span class="v">"Hashem rejoices in His works,"</span> the aspect of <span class="v">"the work of My hands in which to take pride."</span> Hashem rejoices and is glad, <span class="h">kivyachol</span>, in the greatness of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> He receives from Israel — for this is the essence of His delight and joy. As it is written regarding our <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that we take pride in Him: <span class="v">"in Your Name they rejoice all day... for You are the glory of their strength."</span> For <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is joy. As it is written: <span class="v">"He will beautify the humble with salvation; the devout will exult in glory."</span> And it is written: <span class="v">"I will rejoice greatly in Hashem, my soul will exult in my G-d, for He has clothed me in garments of salvation, a robe of righteousness He has wrapped me, like a groom who adorns himself with pe'er,"</span> etc.</div>

<div class="p">It emerges that <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is joy. This is the aspect of wine that gladdens — which is the wine of the cup of blessing, as it is written: <span class="v">"wine gladdens the heart of man."</span> That is: the wine of holiness — the wine of blessing — is the aspect of joy, the aspect of the totality of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, which is joy, as above. For <span class="mx">"song is said only over wine,"</span> as our Sages <span class="h">zichronam livrachah</span> said on the verse <span class="v">"that gladdens G-d and men"</span> (Shoftim 9), etc. — from here [we learn that] song is said only over wine. And all the songs and praises are the aspect of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that we praise and glorify Him with song and joy and praise and gladness. For Hashem is glorified and exalted through the songs and praises of His nation Israel, in the aspect of <span class="v">"He shall be blessed and praised and glorified and exalted,"</span> etc.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of <span class="v">"I will sing to Hashem, for He is greatly exalted [ga'oh ga'ah]."</span> <span class="v">"Ga'ah"</span> — this is the aspect of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, the aspect of <span class="v">"Hashem reigns, He has clothed Himself in gai'us [majesty]"</span> — i.e. the garments of His majesty and <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. Then it is the aspect of <span class="v">"I will sing to Hashem"</span> — for the song and praise is the aspect of His <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and majesty, <span class="h">kivyachol</span>, as above. Therefore the wine of blessing is the aspect of the totality of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, for upon it all the songs and praises are said — which are the aspect of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — for song is said only over wine, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 3 — The Cup as <i>Malchus</i> and <i>Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. For we must now draw the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is the essential <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, the aspect of <span class="v">"and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless... for the land,"</span> etc. The essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is drawn through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, etc., as above. Therefore one must bring a cup for <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, for the cup of wine of blessing is the aspect of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and joy, as above — through which the essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> [is drawn], as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of: the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — one must place one's eyes upon it. For the essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is drawn through the eyes, through gazing upon the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — through which, wherever one gazes, <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed, as above. Therefore one must place one's eyes upon the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. For the wine of blessing — wine that gladdens — is the aspect of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, as above. Through gazing upon this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed — which is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, the aspect of the cup of blessing, as is known.</div>

<div class="p">For the cup of blessing is the aspect of Dovid, the aspect of <span class="v">"I will raise the cup of salvations,"</span> the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span> — which is the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, as above. It emerges that the cup of blessing filled with holy wine — this is the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> that receives the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of Israel, from which the essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> [derives], as above. For the wine in the cup is the aspect of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, the aspect of joy, as above. And the cup itself, which is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span> — for <span class="h">kos</span> [cup] has the numerical value of <span class="h">Elokim</span>, as brought in the writings of the Arizal — and <span class="h">Elokim</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, as it is written: <span class="v">"and G-d [Elokim] is my King from of old,"</span> etc.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore the cup, which is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, is the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, as is known. It emerges that the cup is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which receives its holiness from the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of Israel, which is the holy wine, the wine that gladdens, in the cup, as above. Therefore one must place one's eyes upon it, for the essential thing depends on the eyes. For through gazing with one's eyes upon the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, one's eyes become the aspect of "the eyes of Hashem," and then wherever one gazes, <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed, as above. Therefore one must gaze with one's eyes upon the cup of blessing, in order to create the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> through this — through gazing upon the wine and upon the cup — through which one draws the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> to one's eyes and in turn draws it to the aspect of the cup, which is the aspect of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. That is: to sanctify the air in the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> through the eyes, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 4 — <i>His'pa'arus</i> Is Revealed at the Time of Eating</div>

<div class="p">All of this is needed after eating, for the eating of Israel is holy. The essential revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is at the time of a holy meal of Israel, as Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes elsewhere: the essential completeness of <span class="h">Malchus</span> is through the eating of Israel, in the aspect of <span class="v">"at the time of eating, draw near here [halom]"</span> — <span class="v">"halom"</span> is none other than <span class="h">Malchus</span>. For His <span class="h">Malchus</span> is revealed through the holiness of Jewish eating, and especially through the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. As Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes in his <span class="h">Sefer HaAlef-Bais</span> (letter Alef, "Eating"): <span class="mx">"Through Birchas HaMazon, Hashem becomes known in the world."</span></div>

<div class="p">The revelation of His <span class="h">Malchus</span> — this is the aspect of the revelation of the aforementioned <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, that which Hashem adorns Himself with Israel. Through this, His <span class="h">Malchus</span> is essentially revealed, for <span class="mx">"there is no king without a nation."</span> Therefore when Israel serves Him and does His will — when Hashem takes pride in them — then His <span class="h">Malchus</span> is revealed, as it is written: <span class="v">"Hashem reigns, He has clothed Himself in gai'us."</span> <span class="v">"He has clothed Himself in gai'us"</span> — i.e. garments of His majesty and <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — then <span class="v">"Hashem reigns"</span> — for the essential revelation of His <span class="h">Malchus</span> is through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> He takes in Israel, as above. (This is the secret of what is written in the writings of the Arizal: that the essential building of <span class="h">Malchus</span> is through <span class="h">Tiferes</span> — understand this.)</div>

<div class="p">It emerges that at the time of eating, the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is revealed — the aspect of the revelation of His <span class="h">Malchus</span> that is drawn at the time of eating, as above. For such is the way of <span class="h">Malchus</span> — to display the wealth of its glory and the preciousness of its majestic splendor at the time of the meal, when the essential revelation of <span class="h">Malchus</span> takes place. As it is written: <span class="v">"when the king sat upon the throne of his kingdom, he made a feast, displaying the wealth of the glory of his kingdom and the preciousness of his majestic splendor,"</span> etc. And <span class="mx">"the kingdom below is like the kingdom above."</span></div>

<div class="p">Therefore our Sages <span class="h">zichronam livrachah</span> said: it is forbidden to eat before praying, as it is said: <span class="v">"you shall not eat upon the blood"</span> — do not eat before you pray for your blood. For it is impossible to eat in holiness without first raising <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and delight before Him. Therefore one must pray first, for the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem takes in Israel is through prayer, which is songs and praises and <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, that we praise and glorify Him. Through this, Hashem is magnified and glorified in all the worlds — that He takes pride in us, that He has such a holy nation that knows, in this lowly physical world, how to glorify and praise Him and pray before Him, as it is written: <span class="v">"And You are holy, enthroned upon the praises of Israel"</span> — that through the prayers and praises of Israel, Hashem is sanctified and glorified in all the worlds.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore before prayer it is forbidden to eat, for it is impossible to eat in the holiness of Israel except through prayer, through which the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of Israel ascends. Then the eating is in holiness, for then all the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is revealed specifically at the time of the meal — through which the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is revealed — through which the essential holiness of eating [is achieved], as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="v">"Go, eat your bread with joy, and drink your wine with a glad heart, for G-d has already accepted your deeds."</span> That is: after G-d has already accepted your deeds — your deeds ascend before Him with pleasure and favor, and He takes pride in them, in the aspect of <span class="v">"and Your nation Israel, they are all tzadikim... the work of My hands in which to take pride."</span> That is: after prayer, when Hashem has already received <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and pleasure and favor from you — then <span class="v">"go, eat your bread with joy,"</span> etc. For then the eating is in holiness, the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, through the revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, through which <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 5 — <i>His'pa'arus</i> Called "Eating"; the Illumination of the Face</div>

<div class="p">This is why the verse calls the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem receives from Israel by the name "eating," as it is written: <span class="v">"I have come to My garden, My sister, My bride; I have gathered My myrrh with My spice; I have eaten My honeycomb with My honey; I have drunk My wine with My milk; eat, O friends,"</span> etc. — which Rashi explains as referring to the pleasure that Hashem receives from the <span class="h">korbanos</span> and the <span class="h">avodah</span> of Israel — see there. For the pleasure and <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem receives from Israel is the aspect of eating, for then the essential revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> takes place, as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is what is written in the <span class="h">Torah</span> <span class="v">"And it was, as they were emptying their sacks"</span> (<span class="lr">Siman 17</span>): that through holy eating, one merits <span class="h">da'as</span>, through which the light of the <span class="h">tzadik</span> shines, who reveals all the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem takes pride in each and every one of Israel, even with the lowest of the low, etc. — see there well. For the revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is at the time of holy eating, as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 6 — "Eat of the Fat Portions and Drink of the Sweet" — <i>Rosh HaShanah</i></div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="v">"eat of the fat portions and drink of the sweet... and do not be grieved, for the joy of Hashem is your strength."</span> For the essential <span class="h">tikkun</span> of holy eating is through joy, which is the aspect of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, as above — the aspect of <span class="v">"the joy of Hashem is your strength,"</span> which is the aspect of <span class="v">"You are the glory [<span class="h">tiferes</span>] of their strength,"</span> etc., as above. Therefore this verse was said regarding <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span>, for on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> the essential revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> takes place, as above. Therefore then the essential revelation of the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> [occurs], as it is written: <span class="v">"the eyes of Hashem your G-d are constantly upon it, from the beginning of the year,"</span> etc., as above. Therefore then the verse exhorts to eat and drink with joy, for the joy of Hashem is our strength — through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> He receives from us then, as above — through which the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed — through which the essential <span class="h">tikkun</span> of holy eating [is achieved], as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 7 — <i>Seudos Mitzvah</i>, <i>Shabbos</i>, and <i>Yom Tov</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of all the meals of <span class="h">mitzvah</span>. For when one completes some <span class="h">mitzvah</span> or some <span class="h">masechta</span> [tractate], one makes a meal. For the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem receives from that learning or from that <span class="h">mitzvah</span> is revealed specifically at the time of the meal, for the essential revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is at the time of a holy meal, as above.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of eating on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> and <span class="h">Yom Tov</span>, which is a very great <span class="h">mitzvah</span>. For on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> and <span class="h">Yom Tov</span>, the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and delight of all the <span class="h">mitzvos</span> and <span class="h">avodos</span> performed during the weekdays ascend, as understood from the words of Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> — as he explains regarding the verse <span class="v">"righteousness shall walk before him"</span>: that on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> ascends before Hashem and He takes pride in it, etc. And similarly on <span class="h">Yom Tov</span>, the joy of all the <span class="h">mitzvos</span> gathers, and then one merits the light of the <span class="h">Panim</span> [Face], in the aspect of <span class="v">"three times a year, all your males shall appear before the face of Hashem,"</span> etc. (as brought in the <span class="h">Torah</span> <span class="v">"Mishra D'Sakkina"</span> in <span class="lr">Siman 30</span>).</div>

<div class="p">Therefore, since on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> and <span class="h">Yom Tov</span> all the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of all the <span class="h">mitzvos</span> that Israel performs ascends and shines — therefore then is the essential holy eating, and then it is a great <span class="h">mitzvah</span> to have abundant meals. For the holiness of eating is through the revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — through which the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is revealed and drawn to that place — from which the essential holiness of eating [derives], as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 8 — "<i>Ma'asai Yadai L'Hispa'ir</i>" → "<i>L'Olam Yirshu Aretz</i>"</div>

<div class="p">Regarding what Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes — that the essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is drawn through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem takes in Israel — this is: <span class="v">"and Your nation Israel, they are all tzadikim; they shall inherit the land forever, a branch of My planting, the work of My hands in which to take pride [l'hispa'ir]."</span> That is, as above: through the aspect of <span class="v">"the work of My hands in which to take pride"</span> — i.e. the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> He takes in us — through this, <span class="v">"they shall inherit the land forever"</span> — through this we merit <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. For the essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — the aspect of <span class="v">"the work of My hands in which to take pride,"</span> as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 9 — Chanukah: Kindling the Light of <i>His'pa'arus</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of Chanukah. For the kindling of the Chanukah light is to draw and reveal the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that which Hashem constantly takes pride in His nation Israel. From there we draw this great light, from which the light of the Chanukah candle is kindled and shines — which is <span class="h">pirsumai nisa</span> [publicizing the miracle] — testifying and publicizing the intensity of the miracles that Hashem performs with us in every generation. All of this is on account of the greatness of His love for His nation Israel, that He takes pride in us in every generation. On account of this, He performs miracles and wonders with us in every generation.</div>

<div class="p">For the wicked kingdom of Greece stood against Israel to make them forget His Torah and to make them transgress the statutes of His will. For they were jealous of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that Hashem takes in us through the fulfillment of the Torah and <span class="h">mitzvos</span>, and they wanted to nullify the Torah, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>. They said: <span class="mx">"Write for yourselves on the horn of an ox that you have no portion in the G-d of Israel"</span> — which is the opposite of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that we take pride in Him, that He is our G-d and we are His nation. They wanted to nullify this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — which is also the aspect of nullifying the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of Hashem, for He takes pride in us. For the one depends on the other, and both are one. For according to the fulfillment of the Torah and <span class="h">mitzvos</span>, and according to the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> and joy that we take pride and rejoice in Him — so too He rejoices and takes pride in us, as it is written: <span class="v">"You have distinguished Hashem today, and Hashem has distinguished you today... to make you supreme... for praise and for a name and for tiferes [glory],"</span> etc.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore when the house of the Chashmona'im prevailed and defeated them, the miracle was performed with the lights of the <span class="h">Menorah</span>, and they established for all generations the kindling of the Chanukah light. For the essential light is drawn from the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that Hashem takes pride in Israel for their good deeds — which is the essential light, as it is written: <span class="v">"And G-d separated between the light and the darkness"</span> — and our Sages <span class="h">zichronam livrachah</span> said: <span class="mx">"'Light' — these are the deeds of the tzadikim,"</span> etc. And as it is written: <span class="v">"the light of the tzadikim rejoices."</span></div>

<div class="p">Therefore from this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, the light of the eyes is formed, as explained in this <span class="h">Torah</span>: that this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> becomes the aspect of <span class="h">tefillin</span> — <span class="h">mochin</span> — and they break through into the eyes, and from there the light of the eyes is drawn — through which the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is formed, as above. For the essential light is drawn from the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — that Hashem takes pride in Israel. Then a great light shines in all the worlds, and all the supernal lights and candles are kindled and illuminated, as stated in the holy Zohar: <span class="mx">"to kindle the lamps and illuminate the lights,"</span> etc. From the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, we draw this holy and awesome light of the holy Chanukah candle — through the intensity of the miracle that Hashem performed with us then — through which it was revealed that Hashem still takes pride in us in every generation, and performs great miracles and wonders for our sake.</div>

<div class="p">Through the revelation of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, all the lights shine, as above. From there we draw the light of the Chanukah candle, as above. This holy light of the Chanukah candle — it is a <span class="h">mitzvah</span> to see it, as our Sages <span class="h">zichronam livrachah</span> said: <span class="mx">"One who sees a Chanukah candle blesses,"</span> etc. And as we say: <span class="mx">"these candles are holy... only to see them."</span> For the essential kindling of the Chanukah candle is to draw below the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, in order to merit to see the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, in order to merit through this to feel the sweet and holy taste of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as explained in the aforementioned <span class="h">Torah</span>: that whoever sees this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — wherever he gazes, the air becomes the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, etc. — and a new longing and intense desire for <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is aroused, as understood from the aforementioned <span class="h">Torah</span>.</div>

<div class="p">For on Chanukah one must draw the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, to rectify the blemish of the <span class="h">meraglim</span> [spies] who brought an evil report about the land and blemished <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as Rabbainu writes in the <span class="h">Torah</span> <span class="v">"Ki Merachamam Yenohagoim"</span>: that according to the <span class="v">"s'lach na"</span> [please forgive] that is achieved on <span class="h">Yom Kippur</span>, so one merits the holiness of Chanukah. For Moshe Rabbainu <span class="h">alav hashalom</span> asked <span class="v">"s'lach na"</span> for the sin of the <span class="h">meraglim</span>, etc. It emerges that on Chanukah one must rectify the sin of the <span class="h">meraglim</span> who spoke against <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Therefore we must now reveal the holy taste of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. And this is accomplished through the kindling of the Chanukah candle — through which the light of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, that which Hashem takes pride in Israel, is revealed — through which the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is drawn to wherever one gazes. For the aspect of <span class="mx">"the air of Eretz Yisrael makes wise"</span> is drawn through the light of the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">tefillin</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the oil of the Chanukah candle, which is the aspect of <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">tefillin</span>, as our Sages <span class="h">zichronam livrachah</span> expounded — for the <span class="h">mochin</span> are the aspect of holy anointing oil, as is known. Through this, the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is drawn to wherever one gazes. Then one feels the taste of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, and one returns to truly yearn for <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Through this, one rectifies the blemish of the <span class="h">meraglim</span>, who brought an evil report about <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Therefore one must see and gaze at the Chanukah candle — in order to gaze upon the light of this <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, which is the aspect of the light of the Chanukah candle — in order to merit through this to form <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> wherever one gazes. Then one will return and yearn for <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. And through this one will rectify the blemish of the <span class="h">meraglim</span> who blemished <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="ts">
<div class="sh">✦ Translator's Summary — §§ 1–9 ✦</div>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>Core equation</strong>: <em>His'pa'arus</em> (Hashem's pride in Israel) → Eyes of Hashem → Holiness of <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> → Sanctification of eating.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§1–3</strong>: The cup of <em>Birchas HaMazon</em> = <em>Malchus</em> = <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>. The wine = <em>his'pa'arus</em> = joy. One must gaze at the cup because gazing at the <em>his'pa'arus</em> creates <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> through the eyes. The <em>tzadik</em> embodies all the <em>his'pa'arus</em>; gazing at him on <em>Rosh HaShanah</em> = gazing at Hashem's pride.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§4–5</strong>: <em>His'pa'arus</em> is revealed at the time of eating. "There is no king without a nation" → eating reveals <em>Malchus</em>. Prayer before eating raises the <em>his'pa'arus</em> first. The <em>lechem hapanim</em> = illumination of the face through eating.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§6–8</strong>: <em>Rosh HaShanah</em> eating with joy = <em>his'pa'arus</em>. All <em>seudos mitzvah</em>, <em>Shabbos</em>, and <em>Yom Tov</em> meals reveal the <em>his'pa'arus</em> of the preceding <em>mitzvos</em>. "The work of My hands in which to take pride" → "they shall inherit the land forever."</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§9</strong>: Chanukah candle = the light of <em>his'pa'arus</em>. Greece wanted to nullify both our pride in Hashem and His pride in us. The miracle in the oil → seeing the candle → feeling <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> wherever one gazes → rectifying the <em>meraglim's</em> sin. Oil = <em>mochin</em> of <em>tefillin</em> = holy anointing oil → <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>.</p>
</div>

